{"id":"eliab","name":"Eliab","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:eliab"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Eliab","text":"To whom God is father. (1.) A Reubenite, son of Pallu (Num. 16:1, 12; 26:8, 9; Deut. 11:6). (2.) A son of Helon, and chief of the tribe of Zebulun at the time of the census in the wilderness (Num. 1:9; 2:7). (3.) The son of Jesse, and brother of David (1 Sam. 16:6). It was he who spoke contemptuously to David when he proposed to fight Goliath (1 Sam. 17:28). (4.) One of the Gadite heroes who joined David in his stronghold in the wilderness (1 Chr. 12:9)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H446","lemma":"אֱלִיאָב","xlit":"ʼĔlîyʼâb","gloss":"Eliab, the name of six Israelites","kjv":"Eliab","count":19,"share":0.86},{"strong":"H4932","lemma":"מִשְׁנֶה","xlit":"mishneh","gloss":"a repetition","kjv":"college, copy, double, fatlings","count":3,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H7992","lemma":"שְׁלִישִׁי","xlit":"shᵉlîyshîy","gloss":"third","kjv":"third, three","count":4,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":15,"share":0.68},{"strong":"H251","lemma":"אָח","xlit":"ʼâch","gloss":"a brother )","kjv":"another, brother; kindred, like, other","count":3,"share":0.14}],"verses":["Num.1.9","Num.2.7","Num.7.24","Num.7.29","Num.10.16","Num.16.1","Num.16.12","Num.26.8","Num.26.9","Deut.11.6","1Sam.16.6","1Sam.17.13","1Sam.17.28","1Chr.2.13","1Chr.6.27","1Chr.12.9","1Chr.15.18","1Chr.15.20","1Chr.16.5","1Sam.1.1","1Chr.6.34","1Chr.27.18"],"related":[{"id":"helon","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.227,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"elihu","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.167,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"shemiramoth","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.13,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"jeroham","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.103,"why":"3 verses are indexed under b